Raspberry jam doughnuts
6
Soft fried doughnuts filled with raspberry jam.
---
Doughnut dough
wheat flour|700|g
fresh yeast|20|g
eggs|2|pcs
soft butter|80|g
powdered sugar|40|g
semi-skimmed milk|150|ml
fine salt|1|pinch
water|140|ml

Raspberry filling
frozen raspberries|200|g
powdered sugar|100|g
water|50|ml

Frying and finish
frying oil|500|ml
wheat flour (for dusting)|50|g
---
Make the raspberry jam: put raspberries, sugar and water in a saucepan.
Cook about 15 min until jam-like, then let cool.

Make the dough: in a bowl, mix flour, salt and sugar.
Make a well, add warm milk and water, crumbled yeast and eggs.
Mix until you have a smooth ball of dough.
Knead for a few minutes until soft and elastic.
Add the soft butter and knead until fully incorporated.
Cover with a cloth and leave to rise 1 h 30 at room temperature.

Turn the dough onto a lightly floured surface and flatten with your palm.
Roll out to 1 cm thick.
Cut out 7–8 cm rounds.
Place on a floured tray, cover and leave to rise 30 min to 1 hour under a damp cloth.

Heat the oil: a small piece of dough should rise without browning too fast.
Fry the doughnuts 3 or 4 at a time, turning halfway, until golden.
Drain on kitchen paper.

Before serving, dust with sugar (or powdered sugar) and fill with jam using a piping bag.
---
Optionally use a mix of berries for the jam.
The dough can be kneaded with a dough hook.
Test the oil with a small piece of dough before frying the doughnuts.
